= Wendan Conference Concludes

After weeks of difficult negotiations with the <span style="color: #0A3161;">Western</span> <span style="color: #C8102E;">realms</span>, the Commonwealth delegation at the Wendan Conference has finally secured a result—though not the one it had hoped for. When talks hit a snag, Goodryke made a dramatic offer: a military alliance with <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>, sealed by an exchange of general staff officers. This only outraged the <span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyrian</span> and deepened <span style="color: #002654;">Ethian</span> mistrust.

<span style="color: #C8102E;">Fulyrian</span> Prime Minister Roderic Penhall tried to salvage the negotiations by proposing the repeal of disarmament clauses. But the new <span style="color: #002654;">Ethian</span> sovereign, [? if left_cartel_france: Edwyn Validar II ?][? if not left_cartel_france: Martyn Validar II ?], rejected this outright—refusing any political discussions and treating the Commonwealth’s offer as an admission it could still pay. Backed into a corner, Goodryke’s delegation was left with no option but to offer a final payment of three billion crowns—in exchange for nothing.

- @lausanne

@lausanne
title: At least we walked away with something.
